{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And I will meet Him thus.</b> Rabbeinu Bekhor explained [that Balaam sought] to nullify from them the blessing of ״כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ״ (Genesis 15:5) and ״כֹּה תְבָרְכוּ אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Numbers 6:23). By this I have seen a resolution to what is derived in Berakhot Rabbah (Bemidbar Rabbah 20:7), where it says that he said 'Perhaps I will strike it' — he sought only to strike from them a twenty-fourth part of sixty myriads, which is twenty-five thousand. And one may ask: what benefit would he have from this, if twenty-five thousand were diminished from sixty myriads? Furthermore, one may scrutinize: why did twenty-four thousand fall through his counsel, neither more nor less? Rather, it is certain that his primary intention was to nullify from them the blessing of ״כֹּה,״ for through this the curses would take effect. Therefore he sought only to strike a twenty-fourth part, in the manner that one deducts from a se'ah a twenty-fourth part (Bava Batra 93b) — so too he sought to strike a twenty-fourth part, which is twenty-five thousand, corresponding to the numerical value of ״כֹּה.״ But he did not succeed, for he brought down only twenty-four thousand — 'until כֹּה' and not 'including כֹּה,' for when he reached the number twenty-five, the blessings of ״כֹּה תְבָרְכוּ״ and ״כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ״ stood in their stead."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The numerical value of כֹּה (כ=20, ה=5) is 25; the comment depends on this throughout. The phrase עַד כֹּה וְלֹא עַד בִּכְלָל plays on 'up to but not including' in the halakhic sense."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:42:56.966196310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}